  data:  # 2e3c
    kind: work_item  # 2e3c
    title: "go: os.File.{Write,WriteString} and bufio.Writer.{Write,WriteString} have no catalogue row -- a write through the handle's own method has no sink (17 sites on six repos)"  # 2e3c
    status: todo_hard  # 2e3c
    priority: 2  # 2e3c
    parent:  # 2e3c
    tags:  # 2e3c
    - catalogue  # 2e3c
    - go  # 2e3c
    - io_boundary  # 2e3c
    isbefore: []  # 2e3c
    duplicate_of: []  # 2e3c
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 2e3c
    pr_ref:  # 2e3c
    description: "FOUND 2026-09-03 in WI-suhug's arm-A census (six Go repositories). The METHOD forms of WriteString on a typed receiver are separate primitives from `io.WriteString`, and two of them have no catalogue row:\n\n    435  strings.Builder.WriteString   in-memory  -> correctly unrowed (crosses nothing)\n     62  bytes.Buffer.WriteString      in-memory  -> correctly unrowed\n     10  bufio.Writer.WriteString      NOT ROWED  -> the write goes wherever bufio.NewWriter's argument pointed (WI-vutav's receiver hop, WRITE side)\n      7  os.File.WriteString           NOT ROWED  -> a file, or os.Stdout / os.Stderr (both are *os.File), or a pipe end\n     68  <untyped receiver>.WriteString              -> refused by design (no module hint)\n\nNeither `os.File.{Write,WriteString}` nor `bufio.Writer.{Write,WriteString,Flush}` appears in go.yaml's fs_write section, so a program that opens a file and writes through the handle's own methods has NO write sink at all today (the only rowed write is the free function io.WriteString and the os-level helpers). That is a recall gap in the finding-losing direction.\n\nDESIGN (same shape as WI-vutav + WI-suhug, already built): row `os.File.{Write,WriteString}` dual fs_write / logging / ipc_send, `abstains_to: fs_write`, and stamp from the RECEIVER's binding through `_go_receiver_handle_kind` (an `os.Create` handle -> host_path; `os.Stdout` -> std_stream -> logging; an `os.Pipe()` end -> pipe). Row `bufio.Writer.{Write,WriteString}` dual under the four write boundaries, `abstains_to: fs_write`, stamped through the receiver's `bufio.NewWriter(x)` binding -- `bufio.NewWriter` is already in `_GO_TARGET_ARGUMENT_INDEX`, so the receiver hop works today; only the rows are missing. Run the derived rules first (scope gate: `os.File` / `bufio.Writer` join the reviewed receiver-type enumeration; `Write` is already in ambiguous_names, so only the TYPED receiver reaches the rows).\n\nSizing: 17 sites on six repos -- small, but the shape (write through the handle's own method) is the idiomatic Go file write, so the corpus count understates it wherever `f.Write(b)` is used instead of WriteString: census `.Write(` on typed *os.File receivers before deciding priority."  # 2e3c
    fields: {}  # 2e3c
- op: discuss  # 061d
  at: '2026-09-28T08:50:49Z'  # 061d
  by: agent  # 061d
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 061d
  clock: 2  # 061d
  nonce: 061d  # 061d
  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081. PREMISE HOLDS; ONE DESIGN PREREQUISITE IS NOW MET. Record: scratchpad nunab/run.py (six one-file Go repos, WITH a go.mod; shipped io-boundaries, verify-claims and survey).\n\nSTILL UNROWED: os.File.{Write,WriteString}, bufio.Writer.{Write,WriteString,Flush}. go.yaml's io.WriteString note (~line 170) still discloses the two as NOT rowed.\n\nWHAT THE LOSS IS, measured. It is RECALL LOSS, NOT A FALSE ALL-CLEAR. A must_not_exist fs_write claim over a program that writes only through the handle's own method (the handle an os.File parameter, an os.OpenFile result or a bufio.Writer parameter) returns INCONCLUSIVE, not confirmed. go.yaml declares no module_completeness, so no Go module is an examined negative and the coverage gate withholds. The call is disclosed under external_potential (os.File.Write, bufio.Writer.WriteString). It is absent from fs_write, so io-boundaries reports no write and taint has no sink there. A program that also calls os.Create is VIOLATED through the os.Create row: the open is caught, the write is not.\n(An agent ranking on 2026-09-28 called this a clean-verdict defect without running it. That was wrong, and is corrected here.)\n\nSLOT PREREQUISITE, NOW MET: since INV-vusum (#1269) a typed external receiver's slot is <import path>.<Type>. Emitted today: os.File:0-0:Write (from an os.Create local AND from a *os.File parameter), bufio.Writer:0-0:WriteString, bufio.Writer:0-0:Flush. So the rows this item designs would be reached as written. Two exceptions:\n  - With NO go.mod, the fallback branch (go.py ~3460) still stamps the package ('os:0-0:Write').\n  - os.Stdout.Write(b) emits external:0-0:Write, because the WI-jikik package-variable branch does not type os.Stdout. The design's os.Stdout -> std_stream -> logging stamp therefore has no slot to land on. Check this before building that arm.\n\nNEW ADJACENT GAP, not this row: os.OpenFile has NO catalogue row at all (external_potential lists os.OpenFile). Go's flag-based open (O_WRONLY / O_APPEND / O_CREATE) is therefore unclassified at the OPEN, not only at the write. go.py:2661 already names os.OpenFile as a handle constructor for the handle-kind reader. go.yaml has no mode-discriminated rows, so a flag-discriminated row is new design. Filed separately.\n\nNOT DONE: the item's pre-fix census of .Write( on typed *os.File receivers."  # 061d
